WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.090
- [Instructor] We are
told there are 10 students

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.750
in the poetry club.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.380
This week, each student wrote two poems.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.480
What does the expression
10 times two represent

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.170
and they give us some choices.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.210
Pause this video and see
if you can work that out.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.390
All right, so there are 10 students

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:23.810
in the poetry club and each
student wrote two poems.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.900
So I would use 10 times
two to figure out, hey,

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.240
for each of those 10
students, if they each wrote

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.240
two poems, then we have
10 times two total poems.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.270
And if we look at the
choices, that is choice C

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.960
right over here.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.030
If we look at choice A,
the number of students,

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.470
the number of students is 10.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.270
It wouldn't be 10 times two.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.650
And then the number of
poems each student wrote,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.940
well, that's the second
piece of information.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.270
They each wrote two poems.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.010
That wouldn't be 10 times two either.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.760
Let's do another one
of these, a little bit

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.570
different this time.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:59.340
So now we're asked, let me scroll this

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.670
over a little bit, which
problem can we solve

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.780
with three times eight?

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.240
So pause this video and have a go at it

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.513
before we do it together.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.570
All right, now let's read these and see

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.160
if you can solve it
with three times eight.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.130
Ellen has eight pieces of gum.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.150
Fair enough.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.600
She ate three pieces at school.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.260
Hope she didn't swallow the gum.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.750
That could be problematic.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.070
How many pieces of gum
does Ellen have left?

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.460
So would you use multiplication for that?

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.820
The way I would tackle
it, if she has eight

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.080
pieces of gum and if she ate three

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.970
and we wanna figure out how much gum does

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:40.030
she have left, I'm assuming
outside of her body,

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.370
well then I would
subtract three from eight.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:44.800
I wouldn't multiply eight by three.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.460
So I would rule this one out.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.590
That's not going to be my choice.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.050
I'm not going to solve this problem

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.110
with multiplication or at
least by three times eight.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.980
Brendon has eight t-shirts.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.060
Fair enough.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.710
That's about how many I have.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.600
He goes to the store to
buy three more t-shirts.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.920
How many t-shirts does he have now?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.440
Would I solve that with multiplication?

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.273
Well, let's see.

00:02:05.273 --> 00:02:07.320
The way I would solve it
is he has eight shirts

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.010
and then he's buying three more.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.820
I would add three to
figure out how many total

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.010
t-shirts he has.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.460
I wouldn't multiply by three.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.130
So I'd rule that out.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.520
So let's see how choice C is looking.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.760
There are eight chocolates in each box.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.080
Mike has three boxes of chocolates.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.370
How many chocolates are there?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.010
So this is interesting.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.960
So he has three boxes of chocolates.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.200
So let me draw those boxes.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.420
One box, two box, three
boxes of chocolate.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.950
And each of 'em have eight chocolates.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.390
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.730
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:49.820
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.610
Well, yeah, if I wanna figure out how many

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.030
total chocolates there are,
I have three groups of eight.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.990
I would solve that by
multiplying three times eight.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.540
So I like this choice a lot.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.153
Let's do another example.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.500
Here we are told Gerald is going to plant

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.680
a garden this spring.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.150
That's a good thing to be doing.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.510
He plans to have seven plants in each row.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.490
There will be eight rows.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.160
Which expression can Gerald
use to find the total

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.280
number of plants needed for his garden?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.650
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.980
All right, I'll do a
little bit of a drawing.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.530
I'll do it in green
'cause we're talking about

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:29.500
rows of plants.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.510
So seven plants in each row
and there will be eight rows.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.200
So one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.090
Seven plants in each row.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.660
And then we're going to have eight rows.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.040
So let me copy and paste that.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.793
So that's two rows.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.203
That's three rows.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.410
That is four rows.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.610
Getting there.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.103
Five rows.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.973
Six rows.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.483
Seven rows.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:13.350
And eight rows.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.060
So we don't have to actually calculate it

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.450
but the way you could think about it

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.800
is you have seven plants in each row

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.890
and then you have eight rows of plants.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.340
Eight rows of plants.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.460
So if you wanna figure
out the total amount

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.900
you would multiply eight times seven.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.950
And so let's see, that's this first choice

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:30.783
right over here.

00:04:30.783 --> 00:04:32.900
You wouldn't multiply eight
times seven times seven.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.680
And eight plus seven
is definitely not going

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.500
to give you the total
number of plants here.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.030
So yeah, we like using
the eight times seven.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:40.863
And we're done.

